-- Q15223: Financial Statement Ratios [easy/L1]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): In the five-factor DuPont decomposition, the tax burden ratio is calculated as net income divided by earnings before taxes (EBT). This component, consistent with ASC 740-10-50 disclosure analysis, measures the proportion of pre-tax earnings retained after income taxes, where a higher ratio indicates a lighter effective tax burden.
Wrong (A): Total taxes paid divided by total revenue is an effective tax rate on revenue, not a recognized DuPont component.
Wrong (C): Income tax expense divided by EBIT improperly blends the interest burden and tax burden factors of the DuPont model.
Wrong (D): Earnings before taxes divided by net income inverts the correct formula; the DuPont tax burden places net income in the numerator.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 15223;

